        <div class="duo duo--lead rise" style="margin-top: 22px;">
            <div class="panel">
                <div class="panel__bar"><b>how much work do you need?</b><span class="push">4.x · share of a full parse</span></div>
                {# Percentages rather than microseconds. Only one of these three
                     modes saves anything, and how much it saves is the point.
                     parse() and analyze() run the same lex → recognize → reduce
                     on a source the grammar reads in full; it is the mode that
                     drops the reducers. Measured on every input from 10 B to
                     10 KB: Syntax Check lands at 65…67% of a parse on all of
                     them, Tolerant at 99…101%. Each number is the bar beside
                     it, so the two cannot drift apart. #}
                <div class="rows">
                    <div class="rows__row is-self">
                        <div class="rows__name">Syntax Check<em>is it valid, and how far does it get? no reducers run</em></div>
                        <span class="meter"><i data-fill="66"></i></span>
                        <div class="rows__num">66%</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="rows__row is-self">
                        <div class="rows__name">Tolerant Mode<em>the same work, but problems are reported instead of thrown</em></div>
                        <span class="meter"><i data-fill="100"></i></span>
                        <div class="rows__num">100%</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="rows__row">
                        <div class="rows__name">Parse<em>builds the full result, throws on a mistake</em></div>
                        <span class="meter"><i data-fill="100"></i></span>
